==English==
{{was wotd|2008|September|28}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|refractārius||obstinate}}, from {{m|la|refractus}}, past participle of {{m|la|refringere||to break up}}. Originally {{m|en|refractary}}, {{m|en|refractarie}}, but reanalysed after other adjectives in {{m|en|-ory}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈfɹæk.təɹ.i/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-refractory.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-refractory.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æktəɹi|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[obstinate|Obstinate]] and [[unruly]]; strongly [[opposed]] to something.
#: {{syn|en|contrary|q1=inanimates|fractious|Thesaurus:obstinate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1787|year_published=1863|author=[[s:Author:Alexander Hamilton|Alexander Hamilton]]|title=[[s:The Federalist Papers|The Federalist]]|chapter=[[s:The Federalist Papers/No. 16|No. 16]]|page=[[s:Page:Federalist, Dawson edition, 1863.djvu/247|103]]|passage={{...}} in most instances attempts to coerce the '''refractory''' and disobedient have been the signals of bloody wars, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Pickwick Papers|[[s:The Pickwick Papers (Gutenberg edition)/Chapter 26|Chapter 26]]|text=Mr. Weller knocked at the door, and after a pretty long interval—occupied by the party without, in whistling a tune, and by the party within, in persuading a '''refractory''' flat candle to allow itself to be lighted {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Porter Pollyanna|chapter=8|passage=For five minutes Pollyanna worked swiftly, deftly, combing a '''refractory''' curl into fluffiness, perking up a drooping ruffle at the neck, or shaking a pillow into plumpness so that the head might have a better pose. Meanwhile the sick woman, frowning prodigiously, and openly scoffing at the whole procedure, was, in spite of herself, beginning to tingle with a feeling perilously near to excitement.}}
# {{senseid|en|heat-resistant}}Not affected by great [[heat]].
#: {{syn|en|heat-resistant|fireproof}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1855|author=Frederick Overman|title=A Treatise on Metallurgy|page=315|url=http://books.google.ca/books?id=92rCLRxAVzkC&pg=PA315&dq=refractory#PPA315,M1|passage=Pure lime is extremely '''refractory''', but readily fusible if any silex is brought in contact with it; {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} [[difficult|Difficult]] to [[treat]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1949|author=Albert Fields; John Hoesley|chapterurl=http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?tool=pubmed&pubmedid=18131684|chapter=Neck and Shoulder Pain|title=Calif. Med.|section=70(6):478-482
|passage=Many of the vague and '''refractory''' cases of neck and shoulder pain and of migraine may be due to cervical disc disease.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1990|author=H. A. Ring; et al|chapterurl=http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?tool=pubmed&pubmedid=2292696|chapter=Vigabatrin: rational treatment for chronic epilepsy|title=J. Neurol. Neurosurg.Psychiatry|section=53(12):1051-1055
|passage=In 33 adult patients with long standing '''refractory''' epilepsy on treatment with one or two standard anti-convulsant drugs,}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} [[incapable|Incapable]] of registering a [[reaction]] or [[stimulus]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|author=Nobusada Ishiko; Werner R. Loewenstein|titleurl=http://www.sciencemag.org/cgi/content/abstract/130/3386/1405|title=Electrical output of a receptor membrane|journal=[[w:Science (journal)|Science]]|section=130:1405-6
|passage=The production of a generator potential leaves a '''refractory''' state in the receptor membrane {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1970|author=S.S. Barold; et al|chapterurl=http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?artid=487415|chapter=Chest wall stimulation in evaluation of patients with implanted ventricular-inhibited demand pacemakers|title=Br. Heart J.|section=32(6):783-789
|passage=The {{...}} delivery of external stimuli {{...}} delineates the pacemaker '''refractory''' period after the emission of a pacing stimulus and after the sensing of a spontaneous beat.}}

